      "math_academy_id": "q-141044",
      "sequence_position": 31,
      "problem": "Given that $x,y\\in {C}^{3},$ compute the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨x,y⟩$ of the following two vectors.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}3+2i \\\\ 1-i \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}2-i \\\\ 1+2i \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the definition of the standard Hermitian inner product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & ={x}_{1}\\overset{―}{{y}_{1}}+{x}_{2}\\overset{―}{{y}_{2}}+{x}_{3}\\overset{―}{{y}_{3}} \\\\  & =(3+2i)\\cdot (\\overset{―}{2-i})+(1-i)(\\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}})+3\\cdot \\overset{―}{2} \\\\  & =(3+2i)\\cdot (2+i)+(1-i)(1-2\\text{i})+3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =(4+7i)+(-1-3\\text{i})+6 \\\\  & =9+4i.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
